  "slug": "civil-claim-09-mechanism",
  "title": "Third-party intervention (illustrative) — how Party C’s request card, the case file and the parties of the represented relation are related",
  "titleEs": "Intervención de tercero — Mecanismo o relación explicada",
  "category": "civil-claim",
  "categoryName": "Inicio de reclamaciones civiles",
  "motif": "Intervención de tercero",
  "treatment": "mechanism",
  "family": "spatial-mechanism",
  "description": "A spatial composition of the components — Party C (a fictional newcomer), her card (the request to intervene, as supplied) standing in her tray, the case file that represents the procedural relation, Party A, Party B and the calendar. The card comes in from Party C’s side and never fades. Only the supplied relationships are drawn, without arrowheads (a causal link only when supplied) and labelled on their connectors; a tracer follows the supplied order, captioned “Sequence as configured (illustrative)”, while the case file enlarges. At the gather the case file shows one small card per party in the supplied configuration — intervention requested (◆, one frame round all three) or the initial relation (●, one frame round Party A’s and Party B’s) — with its caption. Both are supplied values of equal weight; the request is never shown as granted or refused; no standing test, type of intervention, admission, effect or outcome is shown.",
